{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"relative-evadable-wattlebird","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Discovered by the disposition pass of bug 8a5e (vacuous single-file AST guards).\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep_heldout.py::_step0_names` enumerates\nmutating members across a HARDCODED four-file list under `adapters/jira/`:\n\n    acli.py, acli_graph.py, acli_rest.py, acli_cli_ops.py\n\nThis is NOT vacuous today — the four files hold real members and the completeness assertion\nhas a live denominator — so 8a5e explicitly ACCEPTED it rather than forcing a fix. But the\nlist is pinned the same way the four rotted guards were: a NEW transport module added beside\nthose four would not be swept, and nothing fails the build to say so.\n\nNot a mechanical fix. Replacing the list with an `adapters/jira/*.py` glob makes\n`test_enumeration_completeness_every_step0_name_is_accounted_for` go RED against every member\nof `adf.py`, `outbound_fields.py`, `probe.py`, `comment_limits.py`, `rich_text_codec.py` and\n`backend.py`, each of which must then be individually classified as mutating or NON-MUTATING\nwith a recorded reason. That is a judgement task about the 429 policy surface, not a\nfind-and-replace.\n\nMeasured context (8a5e): `adapters/jira/backend.py` defines `set_relationship` (:217) and\n`add_comment` (:271), both names in `_CLASSIFIED_MUTATING`, and both are one-line pure\ndelegations to `self.transport.<same name>(...)` under an explicit \"delegates to transport\"\nsection. They issue no HTTP call and carry no 429 policy, which is why 8a5e concluded the\nsweep's transport scoping is correct and this is a separate, narrower concern.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The scanned file set is DERIVED (glob or equivalent) rather than hardcoded, OR an\n      anti-drift assertion fails the build when a module outside the list defines a member\n      named in `_CLASSIFIED_MUTATING` and is not a pure delegating facade\n- [ ] Every newly-in-scope member is classified as mutating or recorded in `_NON_MUTATING`\n      with a reason\n- [ ] Mutation check: a new transport module carrying an unswept mutating member turns the\n      guard RED\n\n## Testing\n\n- `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep_heldout.py -q`","id":"81d5-7914-8a3c-411c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Rate-limit sweep's Cloud file list is hardcoded, not derived (8a5e F7)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785911610316283001,"uuid":"2ed2107f-99d0-4c9d-bdf0-d992b7a871dc"}